    <!-- ========================================================================
         SEARCHABLE FAQ ACCORDION
         ======================================================================== -->
    <section id="faq">
      <div class="site-container">
        
        <div class="section-header-split">
          <div>
            <div class="section-eyebrow">Knowledgebase</div>
            <h2 class="section-title">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="section-desc">
              Questions regarding team formation, eligibility, IP ownership, or mentorship? Search our live knowledgebase.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-search-box">
          <span class="faq-search-icon" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: bold;">FIND:</span>
          <input type="text" class="faq-search-input" id="faqSearchInput" placeholder="Filter questions by keyword (e.g. team size, ages 14-26, beginner, IP, stack, mentor)...">
        </div>

        <div class="faq-list">
          
          <div class="faq-item open">
            <button class="faq-question-btn" type="button">
              <span>What is the team size and age eligibility requirement?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer-pane">
              Teams must consist of 2 to 4 student builders aged 14 to 26. High schoolers, polytechnic students, undergraduates, postgraduates, and independent self-taught developers are all eligible. Cross-college and interdisciplinary teams (e.g., designers + engineers) are strongly encouraged.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question-btn" type="button">
              <span>Are beginners welcome, and what if we don't have an idea yet?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer-pane">
              Yes, absolutely! Vistaara is specifically engineered to take curious students and turn them into confident builders. With 15+ dedicated mentors, 3–5 interactive industry masterclasses in Stage 01 (Explore), and pre-configured starter repositories, you'll find ample guidance to discover problems and ship solutions.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question-btn" type="button">
              <span>What tech stacks and developer frameworks are allowed?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer-pane">
              Any modern mobile, web, or backend technology is permitted! Popular stacks include Flutter, React Native, Swift, Kotlin for App Track; and Next.js, Svelte, Vue, React for Web Track. You can use backend runtimes like Node.js, Python FastAPI, Go, or Rust, along with cloud databases (Supabase, PostgreSQL, Firebase) and pre-trained AI APIs.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question-btn" type="button">
              <span>Who owns the intellectual property (IP) created at Vistaara?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer-pane">
              The builders retain 100% ownership of their ideas, code, designs, and intellectual property. Vistaara and its industry partners claim zero equity, zero IP rights, and zero exclusivity over anything you build during the hackathon.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question-btn" type="button">
              <span>How does Stage 04 Demo Day evaluation and judging work?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer-pane">
              In Stage 04, teams pitch a live 3-minute working prototype demonstration followed by 2 minutes of technical Q&A with our panel of startup founders, CTOs, and product leads. Evaluation strictly follows our 100-point rubric: Real-World Impact (30 pts), Technical Architecture & Code Resilience (40 pts), and UX & Demo Delivery (30 pts).
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>


